WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.024
An official record describes one crossing.

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:09.497
Does that tell us whether fish can reach every spawning reach upstream? It is a tempting leap, but a different claim.

00:00:09.497 --> 00:00:15.639
Culvert Cut is a small, locally trained specialist that makes the gap between evidence and conclusion visible..

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:19.127
Here is a real record held out from training.

00:00:19.127 --> 00:00:23.937
The claim says this crossing guarantees an open route to every upstream spawning reach.

00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:25.374
Read the source beside it.

00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:29.521
Passage is recorded, but a verified upstream network assessment is missing.

00:00:29.521 --> 00:00:32.285
Make your own call before revealing either model..

00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:35.608
The base model calls this contradicted.

00:00:35.608 --> 00:00:41.447
Our trained specialist says not established: the snapshot cannot answer the connectivity question.

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:42.936
That distinction matters.

00:00:42.936 --> 00:00:46.571
Missing evidence is not the same as evidence of the opposite.

00:00:46.571 --> 00:00:52.230
Both responses are actual, unedited local generations, with identical instructions and context.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.137
You can inspect the raw output..

00:00:55.137 --> 00:01:01.196
Across one hundred twenty cases from forty unseen sites, the base produced forty correct verdicts.

00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:06.143
After training, that became one hundred sixteen: ninety-six point seven percent.

00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:08.554
Citation format is measured separately.

00:01:08.554 --> 00:01:15.973
This is a narrow, programmatically labeled benchmark, not a claim that the model understands every ecological question..

00:01:16.973 --> 00:01:19.323
The four wrong verdicts are visible too.

00:01:19.323 --> 00:01:21.438
Here the specialist makes a mistake.

00:01:21.438 --> 00:01:28.781
We publish all prompts, records, and outputs so a judge can inspect the limits, rather than relying on a handpicked success..

00:01:29.781 --> 00:01:32.750
The public website replays recorded model trials.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.326
This local mode runs new claims through the actual adapter.

00:01:36.326 --> 00:01:41.416
Select a site, type a claim, and inspect the returned explanation beside its source.

00:01:41.416 --> 00:01:44.870
No external language model service receives the question.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:49.414
Citation checks still do not certify that every interpretation is correct..

00:01:50.414 --> 00:01:59.026
Behind the experiment is a working map of nineteen hundred thirty-one official fish-passage records in the Lake Washington, Cedar, and Sammamish basin.

00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:05.871
Filter crossings, compare total and partial barriers, and explore field notes from Zackuse Creek to the Sammamish River.

00:02:05.871 --> 00:02:09.749
The original report and a public-works briefing are one click away..

00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:22.454
Pipes are only one pressure.

00:02:22.454 --> 00:02:27.325
King County habitat potential and Ecology water-quality assessments add context.

00:02:27.325 --> 00:02:31.770
The first-flush banner is a labeled demonstration, not a chemical sensor.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:41.390
We trained the one-point-five-billion-parameter model on this Mac using a small LoRA adapter, and included the weights, dataset, and reproducible evaluation..

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:47.694
Ask this basin also offers reliable, cited record summaries without loading a model.

00:02:47.694 --> 00:02:51.547
Follow a source, then copy a specific public-works question..

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:57.114
Our lesson is that an environmental AI should show where its evidence ends.

00:02:57.114 --> 00:03:04.667
Culvert Cut combines local records, a measurable training result, and a practical way to question an unsupported conclusion.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:05.763
Follow one stream.

00:03:05.763 --> 00:03:06.920
Inspect one record.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.321
Ask a better question..
